  "question": {
    "text": "If $a, c, b$ are in GP, then the area of the triangle formed by the lines $a x+b y+c=0$ with the coordinates axes is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "JwKet",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qaDXq",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GWtMD",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "lpVRs",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $a, c, b$ are in GP\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad c^2=a b$...(i)\nAccording to question,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/IGkrU0wr51ePLRxTWR_E5mha2CU4XxNUbUIUo1KLP64.original.fullsize.png\"/>\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\therefore \\text { Area of } \\triangle O A B & =\\left|\\frac{1}{2} \\times O A \\times O B\\right| \\\\\n= & \\left|\\frac{1}{2} \\times\\left(\\frac{-c}{b}\\right) \\times\\left(\\frac{-c}{a}\\right)\\right| \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{c^2}{a b}=\\frac{1}{2} [by Eq. (i)]\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
